A.Ks.prototype={
gXK(){return"Hello, visitor! \ud83d\udc4b"},
gXN(){return"My name is Gean"},
gXL(){return"I build cross-platform apps and AI solutions"},
gXM(){return"I am a Computer Engineer from the Federal University of Para\xedba"},
gUw(){return"About me"},
gUx(){return"Skills"},
gX3(){return"What's next?"},
gX2(){return"Get in touch"},
gJz(){return"Light"},
gI1(){return"Dark"},
gZU(){return"Projects"},
gDp(){return"System"},
gZC(){return"Breast Lesion Classification with Deep Learning"},
gZl(){return"In this project, I developed an enhanced Convolutional Neural Network (CNN) for breast cancer diagnosis by integrating radiomic features extracted from mammographic images directly into the classification model. This multimodal approach resulted in a 17% increase in accuracy and a 13% reduction in the false positive rate compared to the model that used only images. The work led to an in-depth academic study, culminating in my Final Coursework (TCC), which demonstrated the potential of combining radiomics with deep learning to significantly improve the detection and differentiation between benign and malignant lesions."},
gZL(){return"Age Estimation in Dental Radiographs with Deep Learning"},
gZu(){return"In this project, I developed a system for age classification in dental images using advanced image processing and enhancement techniques. The solution applies super-resolution with the DeepAI Torch-SRGAN API, increasing the sharpness and detail of the radiographs, and employs sophisticated pre-processing with random cropping, random zooming, and rotation, expanding the data variability and improving the model's generalization. This approach resulted in greater accuracy in dental age estimation, with relevant applications in forensic dentistry and growth analysis."},
gZM(){return"IoT Tracking System with ESP32, GPS, and Flutter"},
gZv(){return"In this project, I developed an IoT tracking system capable of obtaining and monitoring real-time location data by integrating the ESP32 microcontroller with the NEO-6MV2 GPS module. The ESP32 collects the geographic coordinates and transmits them via Wi-Fi to a cloud database, allowing the information to be accessed by a mobile application developed in Flutter. The app displays the device's position on an interactive map, using the Google Maps API for precise visualization. This solution combines low-cost hardware with IoT and mobile technologies, resulting in a portable, accessible, and efficient system for real-time tracking and monitoring."},
gZN(){return"Portfolio"},
gZw(){return"The very site you are looking at now, built with Flutter Web. Developed as a cross-platform portfolio, it uses the latest in the Flutter ecosystem to deliver a responsive and adaptive interface, working perfectly on desktop, tablet, and mobile devices. It also offers support for multiple languages."},
gZO(){return"BeTalent Mobile Technical Test"},
gZx(){return"This project is a solution for the BeTalent Mobile Practical Test, which consists of building a data visualization from a simulated API. The application was developed using Flutter, following the mockup provided in Figma to ensure fidelity to the design and the given requirements."},
gZP(){return"Pong"},
gZy(){return"In this project, I implemented the classic game Pong in a two-player version, using the C++ language along with the OpenGL graphics library. The development involved creating the collision logic between the ball and the paddles, controlling player movement, real-time score updating, and fluid graphic rendering."},
gZQ(){return"Flutter Instagram Clone App"},
gZz(){return"This app is an Instagram clone made to test responsiveness on different device sizes, using the responsive_framework package."},
gZR(){return"Flutter Udemy Clone App"},
gZA(){return"This application was developed with a focus on responsiveness and layout adaptation, offering a consistent experience on mobile phones, tablets, and desktops. The interface was inspired by Udemy's design and dynamically adjusts to the screen size, ensuring usability, legibility, and optimized navigation on any device."},
gZS(){return"Bitmap Image Color Intensity Editor with Assembly"},
gZB(){return"In this project, I developed a program in Assembly (MASM32) capable of processing BMP images and selectively adjusting the intensity of color channels (blue, green, or red) in each pixel. The program performs direct reading and writing of files via system calls, preserving the headers and ensuring safe value limits for each channel. This approach allows for precise control over the image's color composition, demonstrating efficient manipulation of binary data and low-level image processing techniques."},
gZD(){return"Caesar Cipher in Assembly"},
gZm(){return"In this project, I implemented a program in MASM32 capable of encrypting and decrypting text files using the Caesar Cipher, with a configurable key from 1 to 20, offering a simple interactive menu for executing the operations. The program manipulates files directly through system calls, using 512-byte buffers for efficiency, and includes a cryptanalysis function that estimates the correct key based on the frequency of characters in Portuguese, all structured clearly and optimized to demonstrate low-level control over reading, writing, and data processing."},
gZE(){return"Frequency Domain Analysis and Filtering"},
gZn(){return"In this project, I developed digital image and signal processing solutions applying techniques such as the 1D and 2D Discrete Cosine Transform (DCT) for image analysis and reconstruction, and low-pass Butterworth filters in the frequency domain for images and audio signals, solving challenges such as normalization, preservation of relevant coefficients, and attenuation of unwanted components, ensuring accurate and consistent results."},
gZF(){return"RGB Image Manipulation System"},
gZo(){return"In this project, I developed a complete system to open, display, manipulate, and save 24-bit RGB images, implementing RGB-YIQ-RGB conversion, negatives in RGB and in the Y band, m\xd7n correlation with Mean and Sobel filters, and median filter on the Y band of YIQ, in addition to reproducing pattern correlation analyses with masks using advanced functions, solving challenges of color limits, normalization, visualization, and detection of multiple correlated regions, ensuring precise manipulation and consistent results in different image processing operations."},
gZG(){return"To-Do List"},
gZp(){return"In this project, I developed a to-do list application in Flutter, focused on productivity and personal organization, implementing features such as creating, editing, deleting, and marking tasks as complete."},
gZH(){return"Weather"},
gZq(){return"In this project, I developed a temperature query application that obtains real-time weather information from the Open-Meteo.com APIs, implementing HTTP requests, handling JSON responses, and dynamically updating the interface, solving challenges of API integration, data formatting, and intuitive presentation of weather information to the user."},
gZI(){return"Gif Finder"},
gZr(){return"In this project, I developed an application integrated with the Giphy API to search and display GIFs according to user requests, implementing HTTP requests, handling data in JSON format, and optimized rendering of animated media, solving challenges of API consumption, performance, and a fluid browsing experience in displaying the results."},
gZJ(){return"Youtube clone"},
gZs(){return"In this project, I developed an application inspired by YouTube that consumes the platform's official API to search, list, and play videos, implementing authentication, HTTP requests, and dynamic display of multimedia content, solving challenges of API integration, data management, and interface optimization to ensure a fluid navigation close to the original experience."},
gZK(){return"Firebase login"},
gZt(){return"In this project, I developed a Flutter application integrated with Firebase, implementing a complete authentication flow that allows login with own credentials or via a Google account, using Firebase Authentication and secure integration with the backend, solving challenges of session management, security, and a fluid login experience for the user."},
gX1(){return"Email copied to clipboard"},
gXJ(){return"Home"},
gUu(){return"About"},
gZT(){return"Projects"},
gVA(){return"Contact"},
gUv(){return"At the age of 12, I had my first contact with computers, and at 13, I was already working on my own, formatting and installing programs. In 2016, I started programming in C and Java, and as a computer engineer, I learned Assembly and other low-level languages, gaining proficiency in performance, memory management, and code optimization.\n\nIn 2020, during the pandemic, I discovered Flutter and started my first projects as a freelancer, also learning UI/UX design concepts. Today, I have experience in unit, widget, and integration testing, responsive layouts for mobile, web, and desktop, and state management with BLoC, Riverpod, Provider, and native tools like ChangeNotifier.\n\nI have knowledge of clean architecture, clean code, test-driven development, design patterns, and responsiveness. In addition, I work on artificial intelligence solutions, with experience in machine learning, diffusion models, and convolutional neural networks."}}
